      },
      "worked": "The zeroes are $-1$, $2$ and $4$, with $4$ a double zero. For $x\\ne4$, $(x-4)^2>0$, so the sign is determined by $(x+1)(x-2)$.\n\nThe product is positive for $x<-1$, negative for $-1<x<2$, and positive for $2<x<4$ and $x>4$. It is zero at $-1$, $2$ and $4$.\n\nTherefore $-1\\leq x\\leq2$ or $x=4$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
